## Step 2.5: Self-Healing - Backfill Stale Coverage Gaps

**Run this BEFORE tree analysis and before compiling the report.** If Step 2 found stale coverage gaps, backfill them now. This is mutating, so create a SQLite backup first. Prefer the model-backed summarizer when credentials work; if the provider fails or gaps remain, use the local extractive fallback so coverage is repaired during the same run.

```bash
echo "=== SELF-HEALING: Backfill stale summary coverage gaps ==="
STALE_GAPS=$(sqlite3 /root/.openclaw/lcm.db "
WITH per AS (
  SELECT c.conversation_id,
         COUNT(m.message_id) AS msg_count,
         SUM(CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (
           SELECT 1 FROM summary_messages sm
           JOIN summaries s ON s.summary_id = sm.summary_id
           WHERE sm.message_id = m.message_id
             AND s.conversation_id = c.conversation_id
         ) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS uncovered_msgs,
         ROUND(JULIANDAY('now') - JULIANDAY(c.updated_at)) AS days_stale
  FROM conversations c
  JOIN messages m ON m.conversation_id = c.conversation_id
  GROUP BY c.conversation_id
)
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM per
WHERE days_stale > 14 AND msg_count > 10 AND uncovered_msgs > 0;" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)
echo "Stale coverage gaps before backfill: $STALE_GAPS"

if [ "$STALE_GAPS" -gt 0 ]; then
  mkdir -p /root/.openclaw/backups/lcm
  BACKUP="/root/.openclaw/backups/lcm/lcm-before-stalecov-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S).db"
  sqlite3 /root/.openclaw/lcm.db ".backup '$BACKUP'"
  echo "Backup created: $BACKUP"

  node --experimental-strip-types /root/.openclaw/workspace-cto/scripts/lcm-backfill-stale-coverage.mjs --limit 50 --min-days-stale 14 --min-messages 10 2>&1

  STALE_AFTER_MODEL=$(sqlite3 /root/.openclaw/lcm.db "
WITH per AS (
  SELECT c.conversation_id,
         COUNT(m.message_id) AS msg_count,
         SUM(CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (
           SELECT 1 FROM summary_messages sm
           JOIN summaries s ON s.summary_id = sm.summary_id
           WHERE sm.message_id = m.message_id
             AND s.conversation_id = c.conversation_id
         ) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS uncovered_msgs,
         ROUND(JULIANDAY('now') - JULIANDAY(c.updated_at)) AS days_stale
  FROM conversations c
  JOIN messages m ON m.conversation_id = c.conversation_id
  GROUP BY c.conversation_id
)
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM per
WHERE days_stale > 14 AND msg_count > 10 AND uncovered_msgs > 0;" 2>/dev/null || echo "$STALE_GAPS")
  echo "Stale coverage gaps after model backfill: $STALE_AFTER_MODEL"

  if [ "$STALE_AFTER_MODEL" -gt 0 ]; then
    echo "Model backfill did not clear all gaps; using local extractive fallback."
    node --experimental-strip-types /root/.openclaw/workspace-cto/scripts/lcm-backfill-stale-coverage.mjs --extractive --limit 50 --min-days-stale 14 --min-messages 10 2>&1
  fi
fi

STALE_FINAL=$(sqlite3 /root/.openclaw/lcm.db "
WITH per AS (
  SELECT c.conversation_id,
         COUNT(m.message_id) AS msg_count,
         SUM(CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (
           SELECT 1 FROM summary_messages sm
           JOIN summaries s ON s.summary_id = sm.summary_id
           WHERE sm.message_id = m.message_id
             AND s.conversation_id = c.conversation_id
         ) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS uncovered_msgs,
         ROUND(JULIANDAY('now') - JULIANDAY(c.updated_at)) AS days_stale
  FROM conversations c
  JOIN messages m ON m.conversation_id = c.conversation_id
  GROUP BY c.conversation_id
)
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM per
WHERE days_stale > 14 AND msg_count > 10 AND uncovered_msgs > 0;" 2>/dev/null || echo 0)
echo "Stale coverage gaps after backfill: $STALE_FINAL"
```

- If model-backed backfill fails but extractive fallback succeeds, note the provider failure and the fallback in ACTIONS TAKEN.
- If stale coverage gaps remain after fallback, keep severity at WARNING unless retrieval/integrity checks fail.

